      "original_scope": "Independent static elastic-response replay at each recorded source time. Contact and measured inertial loads are separately mapped to supporting midpoint triangles; local nodal couples preserve the actual source-point wrench and rigid virtual work in the fixed undeformed Shell configuration. Deformation changes the applied moment; both its net drift and a sum of uncancelled local drift norms are retained separately. A reported six-mode mass-weighted balance correction makes the free static problem solvable. This does not preserve every nonrigid3D virtual displacement, does not fit a footprint, and is not a contact-history or capped-control rollout. Original PR22 force/stiffness/PCG/integration kernels and the existing dt*external-force adapter are used; no IPC/contact substitution. Rejected and nonfinite states remain in the journal and raw world fields; material corotation is stored instead of a redundant second tensor copy.",
      "scope": "Time norms retain every finite replay, including rejected static states; they are diagnostic field discrepancies, not admitted static or physical accuracy scores. Phase counts retain the exact source outcomes. Moment drift is measured at deformed Shell vertices, with both a net norm and a sum of local norms to expose cancellation. Near-zero denominators, balance corrections and strict relative-force failures stay explicit."
